  ┏━ Try a request ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │ In the agent's container                                                                       │
  ┃ ▸ GET api.github.com/user                     ┃ │ curl -sS -m 20 -X GET -H 'Authorization: Bearer placeholder' \                                 │
  ┃   GET openrouter.ai/api/v1/key                ┃ │     -w '\n__sandbox_status__:%{http_code}' https://api.github.com/user                         │
  ┃   GET pypi.org/pypi/requests/json             ┃ │                                                                                                │
  ┃   GET example.com/                            ┃ │ Body                                                                                           │
  ┃                                               ┃ │ {                                                                                              │
  ┃ Needs ada@example.com's GitHub credential,    ┃ │   "login": "ada",                                                                              │
  ┃ which the proxy gets from Keycard.            ┃ │   "id": 1234567,                                                                               │
  ┃                                               ┃ │   "name": "Ada Lovelace",                                                                      │
  ┃ Enter sends it from ada@example.com's agent,  ┃ │   "company": "Example",                                                                        │
  ┃ with no credential. The egress proxy asks     ┃ │   "public_repos": 12                                                                           │
  ┃ Keycard for one and adds it.                  ┃ │ }                                                                                              │
